xy124: on the latest ubuntu version some of the dependencies seem to break the build...
(multiple definition of pipapo...)

so a solution is to compile in a docker container with ubuntu focal

the following docker file works

Dockerfile: (i3-compiler/Dockerfile)
```

FROM ubuntu:focal

RUN apt update && DEBIAN_FRONTEND=noninteractive TZ=Europe/Berlin apt install -y git build-essential libxcb1-dev libxcb-keysyms1-dev libpango1.0-dev libxcb-util0-dev libxcb-icccm4-dev libyajl-dev libstartup-notification0-dev libxcb-randr0-dev libev-dev libxcb-cursor-dev libxcb-xinerama0-dev libxcb-xkb-dev libxkbcommon-dev libxkbcommon-x11-dev autoconf libxcb-xrm0 libxcb-xrm-dev automake libxcb-shape0-dev
```

on host:
```
podman build -t i3-compiler i3-compiler/
podman run --rm -it -v ./i3:/i3 i3-compiler
```

in docker container:
```
cd /i3
rm -rf build
mkdir build
autoreconf -i
cd build
../configure
make -j8
```

to install: copy i3/build/i3 to /usr/bin
copy too i3/build/i3/i3-msg to /usr/local/bin

then: https://feeblenerd.blogspot.com/2015/11/pretty-i3-with-xfce.html
